big-spending side
as they open the WSL season on Friday night, when the two-time Ballon d=E2=
=80=99Or winner Alexia Putellas will answer the question of whether she can=
 =E2=80=9Cdo it on a Friday night in Bromley=E2=80=9D.

The London City manager Eder Maestre has the enviable job of being able to =
put together his dream team, but the unenviable job of trying to gel a side=
 that have had 13 departures and eight players coming in. The decision to r=
emove the manager that led them into the WSL, Jocelyn Pr=C3=AAcheur, was bi=
lled as a purely football one by sources, with the club sixth in the league=
 in their first season in the top flight. That decision, though, shows Kang=
 will not accept mediocrity and the patience required by Maestre may not be=
 forthcoming.

Tottenham and Brighton are two other teams aiming high. Martin Ho=E2=80=99s=
 Spurs are the league=E2=80=99s not-so-dark dark horses, with a hugely impr=
essive debut season for their manager followed by an astute and targeted tr=
ansfer window, which has included the recruitment of the third-highest scor=
er in the league last season, the midfielder Kirsty Hanson, and the club-re=
cord signing Alice Sombath from OL Lyonnes.

